  and he rented out this restaurant right  near the hotel  that the team went to in seattle and  teddy bridgewater  had a it was a night for the guys okay  everybody on the t he invited the whole  team  and i don't know how many came 40 or 50  let's say it was a night for the guys  and he said hey listen he got up  and he made a speech and he said i am  not drew brees  i'm teddy bridgewater but i'm gonna give  you everything that i have  to make sure that we do not collapse  that we don't  we don't you know miss a step and of  course they went out and  and beat seattle that week played very  well in drew brees's absence  so that when he came back they were in  pretty good shape  and look here's the one thing that  worries me teddy bridgewater versus  jameis winston  if indeed winston gets the start okay  we don't know right now if jameis  winston is  is turnover jameis you know even though  he has gotten an entire presid  training camp and and whatever 10 weeks  of the season  getting it drilled into him by sean  payton  you know take care of the football all  that we just  don't know yet mike whether uh jameis  winston  is going to be an efficient player and  the other thing we don't know  if let's say they give a game to take  some hill we've never seen that either  we've seen the tantalizing examples  of taysom hill but we haven't seen him  play four  quarters so i'm really really  interested to see how the saints play  this  and look his teammates i can tell you  this mike  his teammates love jameis winston  he has become a big team guy  and inside the team they look at them  they've totally accepted them  they love having them on the team so i'm  very curious to see how peyton handles  this  he's he said today he wasn't going to  announce who was going to start  and good for him why would he  yeah here's the thing though and i i try  to apply a very basic linear approach  because that's how my brain most easily  operates last year that  officially unofficial depth chart that  every team publishes on its website and  then spends the full season down playing  last year it was drew brees one teddy  bridgewater two  taysom hill three this year all year  long  it's been breeze hill winston  hill is the next man up so peter we hear  it all the time next man up next man up  next man up is it x-men up or is it next  man  after that's what's fascinating to me  and here's the other thing too this is a  point sims made earlier today on pft  live  when bridgewater was the starter last  year for five weeks the taysom hill  package  went away because hill's now the backup  quarterback he's not the jack of all  trades  so you're losing the hill package either  way  the question is is hill the starting  quarterback  or is hill the understudy in the event  that jameis gets blown up and can't  continue  so i look they paid hill all that money  we've heard comparisons to steve young  by sean payton let's see what this guy  can do  let's respect the depth chart and let's  put him out there let's find out once  and for all whether or not he can be the  guy  after drew brees and i think if he's not  maybe they already know the answer  yeah i mean i think sean payton is going  to look  at his team this week  and he's going to say how do we play the  how do we use  the quarterbacks we have on our roster  to give us the best chance to win  i do not think that he's thinking hey  what do we have here  i think he's thinking let's try to beat  the atlanta falcons  and not and not be thinking about  opening day 2021.  so mike i i agree i'd love to be able to  see him  and i'd love to be able to see uh  whether he's  really really good or whether he's got a  lot of pock marks on his game  i don't think that's what peyton is  thinking and that schedule  we had it up there there's only  one game that stands out with the  proverbial sore  thumb and that's against the chiefs but  they have that one at home then there's  christmas day against the vikings and  the vikings have had their number in the  postseason in recent years  not in the regular season those are the  two back to back again both at home  and look at that what this is a weird  end of season for the saints peter once  they play the falcons this weekend  they're on the road for four their last  six with those last two back-to-back at  home i  i see five wins there regardless of  who's playing quarterback  and maybe they can even win six maybe  they can find a win  a way to win all seven if brees is back  by week 15.  mike it's why today in my column i said  and i realize it's absolutely  ridiculously premature  but why not i said how about  on sunday of our sat  let's say saturday night of wild card  weekend  the prime time game on saturday night  wild card weekend  tom brady in a rematch at the new york  giants  and you know because it's going to be i  think  i think look you know that the nfl let's  just say  let's just say there are six wild card  games and not eight  okay but if there are six wild card  games  they're gonna put the two games that  have the chance to get the highest  numbers  in those two prime time slots saturday  and sunday  one of them is going to have tom brady  in it  all right and i just think how hilarious  it would be  after 2007 and after 2011  if tom brady was staring down the barrel  of the new york football giants  to advance in the playoffs on the road  the new york football giants in what  might be an  awful bad weather day on january 9 or  10.  i just find that totally delicious  quite honestly i think it'll be so much  fun to see  i hadn't thought of that but that's the  way it's potentially shaping up a lot of  football to be played between now and  then but that's the one i'm now  officially rooting for for wild card  weekend saturday night  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights  from nbc sports

